Z||000000||1FieroGTRacingInc||10-20-2000||11:16 AM||||Well.....  I was going through a intersection and a 99 Chevy Dually pulled out and totally T-Boned me in the pass. door......  BOOM.... that threw me into on coming traffic...  Then  another BOOM  was the 2000 Cavalier that hit me Head on....  my 87 GT IS TOTALLED.....   <P>The police said that it was his fault, and it was a company truck ....  So the police said that His insurance would pay for all 4 of the car's that were involved.....  <P>I guess what I need to know is how much do you all think I will get for a TOTALLED 87GT???  Thank ya'll       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">    Steve||||reg||8
Z||000001||Old Lar||10-20-2000||11:38 AM||||Not enough to replace the car if was in good shape.  Look up in the Kelly Blue book site for estimate of value. I would expect if you are lucky $4K less deductible.<P>Too Bad.||||reg||13
Z||000002||Raydar||10-20-2000||11:39 AM||||Jeeeez, Dude! You okay?<BR>Based upon stuff that I've read, I'm gonna guess $3500 or better. Since it's <I>his</I> insurance, there should be no deductible. I know there are web sites that will give you a value, but I don't know where they are, right now. <BR>If you think they are trying to screw you, just refuse to settle. Their priority is to dispose of the claim. If they see that you are going to hold out, they will give you a reasonable amount, just to close the claim. <BR>You also might start telling them how bad your back is starting to hurt.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ( J/K, unless it really is.) <BR>Be thankful it wasn't a gov't vehicle. You can't get <I>any </I> justice from those bastards. <P><BR>------------------<BR>Raydar<P>Out of my mind.<BR>Back in five minutes.<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 10-20-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||2xsess||10-20-2000||11:40 AM||||OMG...That sucks so bad. I guess you fared ok though. no injuries? <P>Hopefully you'll get enough from the insurance to get an 88GT. <P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>85GT||||reg||1
Z||000004||Wade87GT||10-20-2000||11:43 AM||||So glad to say you can write about and I hope nobody was hurt. But sad for you loss too. Fieros are tough little cars. Hopefully the insurance company will treat you right so you can aquire another (I couldn't use the word "replace").||||reg||9
Z||000005||1FieroGTRacingInc||10-20-2000||12:13 PM||||Yes ....  I'm OK....  the lady that I hit head on(40mph)... was shaken up and had some burn's on her arm's from the airbag, but she's ok though....  thank you all for the information... I'll look it up in the Kelly Blue book...  Thank's...  Steve<P>P.S. Yesssss I'm looking for another GT(87-88)... I'm only buying another Fiero...or I'll just walk to work until I find one.... I'm not driving anyting but a Fiero....  I'm REALLY STUCK ON THESE FIERO'S...  <P>P.S.S......The Fiero was hit square in the door.... that metal brace in the door held up great like it was suppose to.....  <P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||wkayl||10-20-2000||12:21 PM||||You don't have to settle for what their insurance company offers.  If you don't think it is enough, just take the driver of the truck to small claims court (depending on what your states limits are).  Make sure you have documentation of replacement value.  Not only what people are advertizing their cars for but the actual sale price.  Have all documentation of the accident including pictures if possible.  I carry a disposable camera in all my vehicles. I even had my video camera along once when a guy hit me in a parking lot.  The police wouldn't come when they found out it was on private property.  His insurance disputed the claim untill they they recieved a copy of it in the mail.  Good luck ||||reg||1
Z||000007||stsmithgt||10-20-2000||01:30 PM||||Don't be modest about your injuries. If your typing this out with your nose you can say so.  Then I'll only ask yes or no questions. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Sorry to here about your mishap.  Has your doctor refered you to a physical therapast to check for stiff muscles? Having headaches? Hold out for the highest dollar!  Good luck||||reg||13
Z||000008||1FieroGTRacingInc||10-20-2000||02:29 PM||||Thank's Everyone....  I am fine,REALLY!!!!I got out of working today..lol <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Serious, My right shoulder hurt's a little, feel's more loke the joint, more than the muscles. I think it is from stiffing up after the truck hit me, and before I did the head-on dance with the Cavalier...<BR>I feel SOOOOOOOO LOST WITHOUT MY GT!!!!!!!!!!  <BR>But I'll get another one!!!!  OR I'll walk!!!<BR>I just got back from the wrecker place and OMG....  My baby IS TOTALLED FOR SURE!!!<BR>The radiator is in the front truck compartment and, the passenger side dash is pushed toward the REAR of the car about 2 inches and all the sus. and steering component's are totally broken off either at the wheel part or the frame part... pass. door gone,ront fender gone, side scoop section gone, the quarter window gone,front section above the side scoop on the GTclip is history not to mention both wheel's were actually ripped apart at some point...lol and crying at the same time!!!!!<BR>I'm lol because I keep thinking about the NEXT fiero I'll be getting with the insurance$$$!!<BR>Should I get a cheap Fiero and spend 3,500-4,000 on the torque..lol<BR>OR  Should I go and get a high tourqe Fiero with the $$ lol...  what do ya'll think????<P>I am getting a headache though a little...  going to take a tylenol or something..<BR>Thank's soooo much for the concern's of my health   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">.....<P>                I need's opinion's on what to do... <BR>  <BR>P.S.   I miss my GT   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">   &lt;----ME<BR>||||reg||12
Z||000009||Philphine||10-20-2000||03:19 PM||||are you in a fairly big city? here you can get  a fairly decent 4cyl. for a few hundred bucks. if you can find one and not let it drain you (starting mods and/or repairs), you can beat around in it till you find a gt. then you'd have a beater, parts car, hand me down car (that gets parts that you take off a better fiero or parts you can save off your wrecked fiero),winter car (if needed), or sell it again (hard to do).<P>see, if you had had 2 fieros all along (like you should), you'd still be sitting (driving?) pretty.  <p>[This message has been edited by Philphine (edited 10-20-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||DaRkLoRD||10-20-2000||04:30 PM||||Ouch!!<P>I'm sorry to hear about the car.. but glad you're ok. it's never good to hear about a Fiero being in an accident.. but think of it this way, in another car you might have been killed..<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||8
Z||000011||webbee||10-20-2000||04:54 PM||||Youch...Head on and from the side! These cars are tough! Sorry to hear about your loss.<BR>Getting a new one is just like shopping for any car. Look for signs of abuse and get the cleanest low milage one you can afford. Hope you find one soon! Take care of your injuries. You may have concussion, so check with that medical man. Don't forget the lawyer, he may find you have more injurys, too.  ||||reg||1
