Z||000020||Seanh||10-21-2000||11:11 AM||||Glad to hear you came out of it in good condition. A couple of years ago, they were replacing a brige here. They were only doing one at a time (2 two lane bridges) and we were sitting stoped in traffic on the top of one, a uhual truck slammed into the pickup behind us and they hit us. This was in an 84 Lincoln towncar, those things a like solid steel, before they started making new cars from tin foil. The truck was going 40 in a 24 zone. The truck behind us was totaled with a bent frame and our car would have not been worth it to fix. The uhaul however suffered a broken bumper and possibly a new radiator. He didnt get any tickets for speeding or wreckless driving. Doesnt seem fair. We are still going to a ciropractor (sp?) at least once a week and paying out of pocket because the insurance deductable. Make sure, if you dont settle for what the insurance offers (we didnt), you think of what you might need in the future and make sure he pays dearly for his careless actions. As for what car you should get, that depends on what you like doing. If you enjoy working on it and performing the upgrades and engine rebuilds/swaps, then get a basic one. If you really hate doing it, get one already built up if you can find and afford it. I have to get my car appraised once a year just to be on the safe side, so if I do get in a wreck, they know how much I have put into the car. Try and find any reciepts you might have for stuff you have put on the car to increase the value. Also, make sure you include the hours of work youve done to that car. I know how bad settling with insurace can be, been there, done that. But then other times, they give you alot more then the car is valued at with out any hassle or fuss about it. Guess it depends on his insurance company.<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
Z||000021||Loki||10-21-2000||11:20 AM||||DUDE!!!!  That just blows donkey balls.......But hey, ive finally decided tyhings happen for a reason. Maybe it was about to die????   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">   Hell mine broke, and maybe fir a reason. Now im gonna make it better than before.......Hope its all good for ya mna, and I may be around tommorow to work on mine, ill email ya...<P>Loki<BR>ICQ # 16477998<BR>E-Mail  Loki137@Home.Com<BR>Web Page  <A HREF="http://WWW.COX-INTERNET.COM/FIERO" TARGET=_blank>WWW.COX-INTERNET.COM/FIERO</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000022||1FieroGTRacingInc||10-21-2000||12:05 PM||||XTREME..... I saw the post on the black 88 gt, when I was looking at contra's 87GT....<BR>But I'll have to see what the insurance does on it...  I just spent what little that I had saved on the car, shaving my mirror's off and was fixing to do the door handles.. and doing a little to the motor's trying to get it running good...<P>seanh... sorry to hear about your bad luck with the U-haul...  I look for reciept's today, I'm going to put a good set of seat cover's on there today --to look a little better for the insurance man..lol<P>Loki...  hey dude, glad to hear from you...  e-mail me at  atyeo at tyler.net   AND yes  EVERYTHING HAPPEN;S FOR A REASON --GOD say's so--  I will have an even better GT then my ..sniff,sniff   my 87GT... <P>thank everyone for the help... THAT'S WHAT FIERO FREAK'S ARE FOR...  he he he<BR>                    Steve||||reg||6
